WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:02.380
How do regular expressions describe

2
00:00:02.380 --> 00:00:05.000
languages? A regular expression is

3
00:00:05.000 --> 00:00:07.240
syntax assembled from small expressions,

4
00:00:07.240 --> 00:00:08.940
while its language is the

5
00:00:08.940 --> 00:00:10.220
set of words that syntax

6
00:00:10.220 --> 00:00:12.880
describes. We will build expressions

7
00:00:12.880 --> 00:00:14.260
from their meanings and check

8
00:00:14.260 --> 00:00:16.000
short boundary cases instead of

9
00:00:16.000 --> 00:00:17.040
trusting their appearance.

10
00:00:17.580 --> 00:00:19.660
The atomic expression a describes

11
00:00:19.660 --> 00:00:21.860
the singleton language containing a.

12
00:00:21.860 --> 00:00:24.500
Epsilon describes the singleton containing

13
00:00:24.500 --> 00:00:26.400
the empty word, whereas the

14
00:00:26.400 --> 00:00:28.720
empty-set expression describes no words.

15
00:00:29.220 --> 00:00:31.000
These are different base cases,

16
00:00:31.360 --> 00:00:32.280
even though both of the

17
00:00:32.280 --> 00:00:33.620
latter may involve no visible

18
00:00:33.620 --> 00:00:34.320
input symbols.

19
00:00:34.740 --> 00:00:36.280
Union chooses a word from

20
00:00:36.280 --> 00:00:39.220
either operand language. Concatenation chooses

21
00:00:39.220 --> 00:00:40.940
one word from each operand

22
00:00:40.940 --> 00:00:42.520
and joins them, while star

23
00:00:42.520 --> 00:00:44.620
chooses zero or more operand

24
00:00:44.620 --> 00:00:46.840
words. In the usual precedence

25
00:00:46.840 --> 00:00:48.940
convention, star binds most tightly,

26
00:00:48.940 --> 00:00:51.220
followed by concatenation, then union.

27
00:00:51.820 --> 00:00:53.700
Expand the expression zero or

28
00:00:53.700 --> 00:00:56.200
epsilon, followed by one or

29
00:00:56.200 --> 00:00:58.440
epsilon. There are four combinations

30
00:00:58.440 --> 00:01:00.800
of choices, producing epsilon, zero,

31
00:01:01.060 --> 00:01:02.400
one, and zero one. The

32
00:01:02.400 --> 00:01:03.800
result is not all binary

33
00:01:03.800 --> 00:01:04.900
words of length at most

34
00:01:04.900 --> 00:01:06.840
two, because one zero and

35
00:01:06.840 --> 00:01:08.780
the repeated-symbol pairs are absent.

36
00:01:09.460 --> 00:01:11.260
To describe words that begin

37
00:01:11.260 --> 00:01:12.600
with one and end with

38
00:01:12.600 --> 00:01:15.160
zero, place an arbitrary binary

39
00:01:15.160 --> 00:01:17.640
string between those endpoints. The

40
00:01:17.640 --> 00:01:19.660
expression one Sigma star zero

41
00:01:19.660 --> 00:01:21.460
includes one zero by choosing

42
00:01:21.460 --> 00:01:23.240
the middle word empty. It

43
00:01:23.240 --> 00:01:24.860
excludes words of length one,

44
00:01:25.180 --> 00:01:26.560
which is correct because a

45
00:01:26.560 --> 00:01:28.160
single symbol cannot be both

46
00:01:28.160 --> 00:01:29.400
those different endpoints.

47
00:01:29.900 --> 00:01:31.560
For words beginning and ending

48
00:01:31.560 --> 00:01:33.580
with the same symbol, endpoint

49
00:01:33.580 --> 00:01:35.460
wrapping alone misses a boundary

50
00:01:35.460 --> 00:01:37.740
case. Zero Sigma star zero

51
00:01:37.740 --> 00:01:39.320
or one Sigma star one

52
00:01:39.320 --> 00:01:41.140
handles lengths at least two,

53
00:01:41.540 --> 00:01:43.180
but the one-symbol strings zero

54
00:01:43.180 --> 00:01:45.640
and one also qualify. Add

55
00:01:45.640 --> 00:01:48.420
those two alternatives explicitly, while

56
00:01:48.420 --> 00:01:50.740
epsilon remains excluded because it

57
00:01:50.740 --> 00:01:52.020
has no first symbol.

58
00:01:52.500 --> 00:01:53.920
At least three ones can

59
00:01:53.920 --> 00:01:55.860
be expressed by three required

60
00:01:55.860 --> 00:01:57.960
ones separated and surrounded by

61
00:01:57.960 --> 00:02:01.240
arbitrary binary strings. Those arbitrary

62
00:02:01.240 --> 00:02:03.280
parts may contain more ones,

63
00:02:03.560 --> 00:02:04.640
which is exactly what at

64
00:02:04.640 --> 00:02:06.820
least permits. Replacing them all

65
00:02:06.820 --> 00:02:08.840
with zeros-only stars would impose

66
00:02:08.840 --> 00:02:11.100
an unnecessary restriction on where

67
00:02:11.100 --> 00:02:12.460
extra ones may occur.

68
00:02:13.020 --> 00:02:15.480
The tutorial comment language illustrates

69
00:02:15.480 --> 00:02:17.360
a more delicate boundary condition.

70
00:02:17.800 --> 00:02:19.240
A word must have disjoint

71
00:02:19.240 --> 00:02:21.860
opening slash-hash and closing hash-slash

72
00:02:21.860 --> 00:02:24.340
delimiters, with no hash-slash inside

73
00:02:24.340 --> 00:02:26.500
the content. Therefore an empty

74
00:02:26.500 --> 00:02:28.120
comment still needs four symbols,

75
00:02:28.120 --> 00:02:30.060
and an early closing delimiter

76
00:02:30.060 --> 00:02:31.500
cannot be ignored just because

77
00:02:31.500 --> 00:02:32.620
another appears later.

78
00:02:33.060 --> 00:02:35.100
Use identities only when their

79
00:02:35.100 --> 00:02:37.840
language meanings justify them. Union

80
00:02:37.840 --> 00:02:39.640
with the empty language changes

81
00:02:39.640 --> 00:02:42.680
nothing, concatenation with epsilon changes

82
00:02:42.680 --> 00:02:44.880
nothing, and concatenation with the

83
00:02:44.880 --> 00:02:47.420
empty language destroys every possible

84
00:02:47.420 --> 00:02:49.240
pair. Star of the empty

85
00:02:49.240 --> 00:02:51.200
language is the singleton epsilon

86
00:02:51.200 --> 00:02:53.340
because zero factors are still

87
00:02:53.340 --> 00:02:53.800
allowed.

88
00:02:54.220 --> 00:02:55.540
Things to take note of.

89
00:02:56.000 --> 00:02:57.780
Translate each operation into a

90
00:02:57.780 --> 00:02:59.920
choice of words, respect operator

91
00:02:59.920 --> 00:03:02.060
precedence, and test epsilon and

92
00:03:02.060 --> 00:03:04.280
shortest words. Expressions that look

93
00:03:04.280 --> 00:03:05.820
different can describe the same

94
00:03:05.820 --> 00:03:08.760
language; examples alone suggest equivalence,

95
00:03:08.980 --> 00:03:10.680
while a construction or two-way

96
00:03:10.680 --> 00:03:12.240
language argument proves it.
